  "_doc": "Task 57: weapon items (written by the reviewer; the builder wires the code). Each weapon is an inventory item. Using one never adds new combat mechanics: it feeds the existing systems. In a fight, threat or robbery (PersonActs, SkillCheck) the weapon adds `check` to the actor's skill, raises the injury through Health.injure by `injury_step` (capped at 3, severity 3 = hospital, and the existing crime and health systems decide what happens next), and makes the case charge more serious (`charge`). `intimidate` adds to threats and demands. `noise` feeds Notice (how far it is heard). `conceal`: pocket / bag / none (always visible). `legal`: free | permit | banned; carrying without the permit or a banned item is its own charge (`carry_charge`). `evidence`: what it can leave for a case (prints, blood_trace, casing, ballistics). `sources`: where it can be bought or found; `price` in coins; `ammo` names its ammunition item (a gun without ammo uses the `empty` stats). `model`: the Blender model name in assets/models. `skill`: the skill used (fighting or shooting). `mishap`: the catastrophe id (54) when an attempt goes very wrong.",
